# Security

Treat all client input, device input, webhook input, uploaded files, and external API responses as untrusted.

Every mutation must be authorized.

Protect against IDOR, cross-tenant access, mass assignment, SQL injection, XSS, CSRF, SSRF, path traversal, command injection, replay, and unsafe file uploads.

Use secure password hashing and framework authentication.

Use least privilege for roles and service credentials.

Never store raw card data or CVV. Payment providers must tokenize sensitive payment information.

Verify webhook signatures and make webhook processing idempotent.

Encrypt sensitive credentials at rest and use TLS in transit.

Camera/device credentials must never appear in logs or API responses.

LPR evidence and plate data must have configurable retention and access controls.

Security-sensitive operations must produce audit events.

When reviewing code, prioritize security and tenant isolation before style.
